  "body": "Independent native fused Q/K RMSNorm + RoPE HIP validation for both rotary layouts, Q32/K8/V8 heads, width128, block256/wave64 with logical32 reductions.\n\nBoth AMD hosts completed 48 paired trials (96 launches each), with fresh CPU float64/Torch FP32 audits of 79,626,240 values: zero tolerance failures and zero adapted/upstream bit differences. The 3,948 differences from rounded Torch FP32 are retained in the audit. Inputs, weights, gathered cache, positions, allocation guards and upstream V heads are checked unchanged where required. Original upstream kernel/common-helper bodies and the conversion header are retained in the comparison; compiler-reported source/header inputs are captured.\n\nAssets contain all frozen input bytes, both hosts' complete output streams, runtime reports, compiled binaries and compiler input captures. SHA256.json gives hashes and sizes. Source/proof-component revision: c9a7a242de6696e4c9c1aa402d7046b3db2518d9.\n\nThe formal component study binds both full sources and proves address coverage, ownership and bounds. Complete native execution, actual-trace classification and dense-reference equality remain pending; this profile issues zero source certificates. These are independent AMD adaptations, not the authors' original artifacts, model results or NVIDIA measurements. IEEE/error guarantees are outside the paper's formal scope.\n"
